# fixedbugs, defect 2389, 2026-11-09.
#
# SYMPTOM: a group binding a C function named `h0_p`, called where the
# function's first local is `p`, was *internal error* at exit 2: the body
# declared that local `int64_t h0_p;` and the call `t3 = h0_p(t2);` read it.
#
# FIX: reached through its accessor (`emit/shadowed.hero`), so it prints 42.

extern "fixedbugs-2389-a-bound-c-function-named-as-a-local-builds.h"
    function h0_p(v: i64) -> i64

function main()
    p = 40
    print(h0_p(v: p))
